# What must never enter an Esytol image.
#
# The Dockerfile's runtime stage copies three explicit paths out of the builder,
# so this file mainly protects the *build context* — everything sent to the
# daemon, and everything the builder stage can see. A credential in a build
# layer is recoverable even after a later layer removes it.

# ── Credentials and local state ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
pat.txt
PAT.txt
secrets/
.npmrc
.vercel

# ── Source control and CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.husky

# ── Build output and dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────
# `node_modules` is reinstalled from the lockfile inside the image; copying the
# host's would import a tree built for another platform.
node_modules
.next
out
coverage
test-results
playwright-report

# ── Tests and tooling the runtime never uses ─────────────────────────────────
tests
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts
.lintstagedrc.json
eslint.config.mjs
.prettierrc
.prettierignore

# ── Documentation ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docs
*.md
!README.md

# ── Editor and OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.forge
